      "id": "51",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 51,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "がある indicates the existence or possession of something. For example, ペンがある means 'There is a pen (on the table, etc.)' or 'I have a pen.' On the other hand, だ expresses assertion or determination similar to 'is/are' in English. In contrast to the がある example, ペンだ would mean 'It (=the thing we are looking at) is a pen.'",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 13,
          "slug": "がある",
          "title": "がある",
