        "body": "がある expresses the existence or possession of inanimate objects, similar to 'there is' or 'I have' in English (e.g., ピアノがある = 'There is a piano' or 'I have a piano'). When combined with a noun, it describes the noun, much like an adjective (e.g., ピアノがあるレストラン = 'A restaurant with a piano'). Remember, ある changes to いる when referring to animate objects.",
